  "step_1": "The decision reason is based on the skewness of the lotteries, defined as the extent to which a greater portion of the probability is assigned to favorable outcomes (i.e., less negative or zero outcomes) compared to unfavorable ones (i.e., larger losses). In this context, favorable outcomes are those closer to 0 Euros. Lottery A: -3000 with 90%, 0 with 10% → probability of favorable outcome (0) is 10%. Lottery B: -6000 with 45%, 0 with 55% → probability of favorable outcome (0) is 55%. Thus, Lottery B assigns a much higher probability to the favorable outcome (0) than Lottery A. Since skewness here reflects the concentration of probability on the 'better' (less negative) outcomes, Lottery B is more left-skewed than Lottery A. Therefore, the decision reason would prefer Lottery B.",
